  "details": "I know the Button was removed out of the World Tab in the Main Menu so you can see more Categories when first opening that Tab but i don't think this was the right thing to do.\n# My Issue With The Removal:\nI don't think the benefit of seeing one more Category is justifying removing such a Useful Button. It allowed for quick access to the World you are in, to for example create a new Instance, View the World Author, Set it as your Home or get more info about the World. I know there are other ways to get to that page but all of them take longer to reach and people who don't know where those are might not find them. Before you Could just open the QM, click on Worlds and click on the Current World Button, now you always have to do one more step to reach it (e.g. open QM, go to Worlds, go to the Profile Tab, click on the Location) and I don't think that is worth seeing one more Category in that side bar.\nIt also makes it inconsistent with all the Other Tabs, in the Avatar Tab you have a Button for the Current Avatar, in Social you have a button for your Current Status. In those Tabs you always have a button to see your Current \"Setting\" related to that Tab, but you no longer have that for the World Tab.\nIt also makes it harder for users of the old menu to find the current Instance since they are used to find that at the top of the Worlds Menu.\nAlso, just as a side note, I have not seen any canny requesting this to be done so I'm confused why it was removed in the first place without people requesting it.\n# Suggestion:\nWith all of this in mind I don't think it's worth to remove that button just so you can see one more Category when you first open the Worlds Tab, especially since you can just scroll down if you want to see more.\n# Attachments:\nIn the pictures below you can see the Current World missing in the Worlds Tab while Social & Avatars still have info about the current \"setting\" related to it:",
